,title,link,text,language,family
0,Sajau Basap language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/sajau_basap_language,"Sajau Basap is a member of the Austronesian language family, specifically within the Malayo-Polynesian branch. It is part of the Western Malayo-Polynesian languages spoken on Borneo.",Sajau Basap,Austronesian
1,Sajau Basap - sjb (Austronesian) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/sjb/,"Sajau Basap (sjb) is part of the Austronesian family and Austronesian, Malayo-Polynesian, North Borneo, Rejang-Sajau class. Sajau Basap speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts: Types.",Sajau Basap,Austronesian
2,Sajau Basap Language (SJB) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/sjb,"Sajau Basap is an endangered indigenous language of Indonesia. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by a decreasing number of young people.",Sajau Basap,Austronesian
3,Austronesian Lexemes in Basa Latala of Borneo: A Punan Sajau...,https://bahasawan.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Austronesian-Lexemes-in-Basa-Latala.pdf,"(2022) admit that direct borrowings from Punan Sajau are found in Basa Latala but claim they are exceptional in being the only terms with clear Austronesian etymologies, Sajau and Latti terms from Guerreiro (2015) were also compared to the Basa Latala wordlist, looking for matches.",Sajau Basap,Austronesian
